# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large artifacts that were being shipped to the daemon on every build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The QEMU test harness cache. This was the whole story: `docker build .` in a
# tree that has run `make vm-test` sent a 15.1GB context - a 14.4GB provisioned
# guest disk, the 596MB cloud image and a 45MB source tarball - before the
# daemon could read line one of the Dockerfile. It also holds a qemu monitor
# socket, which the daemon cannot put in a tar at all:
#   Can't add file .vmcache/qemu-monitor.sock to tar: sockets not supported
.vmcache/
*.qcow2
*.img
*.iso

# The generated copy of docs/ that Pages publishes, demo GIF included. Nothing
# in the image reads it, and the GIF alone is 2.8MB that changes on re-render.
pages/

# Test sources and fixtures. `go build ./cmd/...` never compiles a _test.go,
# and leaving them in the context meant a test-only commit invalidated the
# COPY layer and forced a full recompile of the image in CI.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/

# Agent and editor state.
.claude/
